{"type":"cards","title":"Runbooks","items":[{"title":"Issue: primary region cluster failure","fix":"Fix: force WSFC quorum on DR node, execute FORCE_FAILOVER_ALLOW_DATA_LOSS, and update Cloud DNS listener TTL.","status":"Amber","text":"Fix: Force WSFC quorum on DR, run failover with data loss, reduce Cloud DNS TTL. Status: Amber"},{"title":"Issue: replica suspended data movement state","fix":"Fix: inspect redo queue DMV, apply missing transaction log backups from Cloud Storage, and run alter database SET hadr resume.","status":"Amber","text":"Fix: Inspect redo queue DMV, apply missing transaction log backups from Cloud Storage, and run alter database SET hadr resume. This clears log stalls and restores replication synchronization. · Status: Amber"},{"title":"Issue: monthly OS and SQL Server patching","fix":"Fix: patch asynchronous DR replica first, patch synchronous secondary second, trigger planned zero-data-loss failover, then patch former primary.","status":"Grey","text":"Fix: Patch asynchronous DR replica first, patch synchronous secondary second, trigger planned zero-data-loss failover, then patch former primary. This ordered workflow preserves active uptime. · Status: Grey"},{"title":"Issue: file share witness loses quorum reachability","fix":"Fix: verify VPC firewall TCP 445 rules, re-bind witness share via Set-ClusterQuorum PowerShell cmdlet, and validate dynamic vote weights.","status":"Grey","text":"Fix: Verify VPC firewall TCP 445 rules, re-bind witness share via Set-ClusterQuorum PowerShell cmdlet, and validate dynamic vote weights. This restores clean witness voting across all nodes. · Status: Grey"}],"notes":"Standardized operational runbooks pair every high-priority failure mode with exact PowerShell and T-SQL remediation commands. Combining Terraform automation with standardized DBA runbooks is proven in retail and enterprise deployments to cut outage frequency and standardize recovery times.

